--TEST--
a `secret` value may be written into an array element or a shape field only where the container's own type carries the qualifier — `rule:security/secret-qualifier` and `rule:errors/record-transformations`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The accepted half is written first and reports nothing: a container that
// declares what it carries is the way to keep a credential, and a value read
// back out of one is still `secret`.
type Keep = {token: secret string};

secret string $token = "literal";
array<secret string> $kept = [$token];
$kept["t"] = $token;
secret string $back = $kept["t"];
Keep $shape = {token: $token};
secret string $field = $shape->token;

// `rule:security/secret-qualifier`: an array literal joins no element types,
// so `array<mixed>`'s own `mixed` is the whole of what would carry the
// qualifier past the bracket.
array<mixed> $bag = [$token];

// The same write one statement later, and one character over: a refusal that
// either spelling walks around is not a refusal.
array<mixed> $later = [];
$later["t"] = $token;
$later["u"] .= $token;

// A shape literal *infers* its field types, so the bit survives the braces
// and stops where the declared field is wider than the value.
type Wide = {token: mixed};
Wide $wide = {token: $token};
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0824]: a `secret` value cannot be stored in an array element: `mixed` keeps no qualifier
   --> case.nvs:17:22
%A
error[E0824]: a `secret` value cannot be stored in an array element: `mixed` keeps no qualifier
   --> case.nvs:22:15
%A
error[E0824]: a `secret` value cannot be stored in an array element: `mixed` keeps no qualifier
   --> case.nvs:23:16
%A
error[E0824]: a `secret` value cannot be stored in the field `token`: `mixed` keeps no qualifier
   --> case.nvs:28:22
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
